WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.140
It's Friday. Welcome to Tesla Short's Time, Daily, Episode 515. I'm Patrick in Vancouver.

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:14.520
Today is June 19th, 2026. Let's see how Tesla is heading into the weekend. Tesla's new

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:22.780
lowest-price Cybertruck trim begins deliveries this week at $59,990. The entry-level Cybertruck

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:31.600
trim at $59,990 started reaching early buyers this week. The model drops certain range and feature

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:37.820
options found on higher trims. It gives Tesla a lower starting price in the pickup segment than

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:43.480
previous configurations. Deliveries will show how demand responds at this new price point.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:50.340
This marks the first real test of volume potential at the revised price level. From pricing pressure

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:56.700
in the US pickup segment, the story now turns to regulatory pressure on autonomy features in Europe.

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:03.620
Danish regulators cleared Tesla's supervised FSD package for use. The approval covers current

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:09.840
supervised operation on public roads. It adds another EU country where the feature can be activated

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:17.280
after local testing. Sweden's transport authority recommended the EU reject the supervised FSD package,

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:23.560
unless the system is altered to prevent exceeding posted speed limits. The stance adds another

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:30.280
national voice to ongoing European reviews of driver assistance rules. The outcome will influence

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:36.580
whether other member states adopt similar restrictions. From European regulatory friction on software,

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:44.400
attention now shifts to a hardware-related legal claim also tied to future FSD capability. A group

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:52.140
of 7,000 HW-3 owners joined a claim alleging hardware limitations for future unsupervised FSD.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:59.060
A law firm has taken on the case for potential collective proceedings. Tesla has not commented on

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:05.480
the specific allegations. The next milestone is whether the claim advances to formal litigation.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:12.380
From questions about existing hardware capability, the focus moves to a new patent aimed at improving

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:19.060
efficiency on future vehicles. Tesla's new design pairs low-rate parallel air springs with series

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:26.080
dampers for most ride duties. The active actuator only corrects when needed, cutting energy use compared

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:33.600
with fully active systems. The approach draws from the 1998 Lincoln Mark 8 air suspension but adds

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:39.560
passive dominant tuning. This could help preserve range on vehicles that already carry heavy battery

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:46.400
packs. Tesla first principles looks at the energy budget trade-offs here. The patent returns to a

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:53.920
1998 Lincoln Mark 8 layout but flips the energy budget. Instead of an always active hydraulic or

00:02:53.920 --> 00:03:00.800
electromagnetic actuator fighting every bump, the design lets passive air springs and dampers absorb

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:07.080
most road inputs. Only the moments that exceed the passive envelope trigger the powered element.

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:13.140
That single change cuts continuous power draw and therefore battery energy that would otherwise

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:19.980
be lost as heat. Every watt kept out of the suspension is a watt still available for propulsion or

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:25.420
climate control. On a vehicle whose mass is already dominated by the battery pack,

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:32.360
even modest reductions in auxiliary loads compound over a full charge cycle. The deeper question is

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:37.720
whether this hybrid passive plus corrective approach scales to the next generation of vehicles

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:44.420
or remains a niche efficiency tweak. From the suspension patent, the episode turns to Tesla's

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:50.360
physical expansion in India and Iceland. Tesla opened a new experience center in Hyderabad

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:56.840
and scaled local delivery and service teams. The move increases physical presence in one of India's

00:03:56.840 --> 00:04:03.140
fastest growing tech corridors. It follows earlier service expansions in other major Indian cities.

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:08.360
Tesla also marked a new operational step in Iceland with expanded local presence.

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:14.800
The development adds another European market with dedicated support infrastructure. It follows

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:21.220
steady growth in Nordic registrations and service coverage. From physical retail and service growth,

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:25.300
the next update covers software side convenience changes for owners.

00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:34.860
Version 4.58.0 introduces charge stats V2, Android live notifications, and a top-down view for the

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:41.980
Tesla semi. Owners can now see more granular charging history and real-time status without opening the app.

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:49.020
The update applies across current vehicle software versions. Release notes list the exact feature

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:55.360
additions. From owner-facing software tweaks, the story moves to a new market incentive that could

00:04:55.360 --> 00:05:02.760
affect sales. The Model 3 qualified for China's 2026 rural electric vehicle purchase incentives.

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:10.880
The list includes 155 models eligible for local rebates and tax breaks. Inclusion could support

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:18.280
sales in lower tier cities where price sensitivity remains high. Tesla has not disclosed expected volume

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:25.880
impact from the program. From policy support in China, the lens widens to a new competitive threat in

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:34.140
the Model Y price band. Patent images show Lucid's planned cosmos SUV positioned near the Model Y

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:41.520
price band. The vehicle targets similar size and utility as the Model Y and upcoming Rivian are two.

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:48.940
Lucid has not released final specs or timing yet. The design filing gives the first clear look at

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:55.920
exterior proportions. From rival product plans, real-world efficiency data on Tesla's own vehicles

00:05:55.920 --> 00:06:04.980
provides a benchmark. Real-world tests measured how closely several 2025 EVs match WLTP range claims.

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:11.780
The Tesla Model Y landed in the middle of the group for achieved versus advertised distance.

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:17.440
BYD models showed both the smallest and largest gaps depending on the variant.

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:23.400
The data covers mixed driving conditions on Australian roads. From efficiency testing,

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:29.700
the final item looks at fleet-level adoption decisions. Green Bay police added Tesla vehicles

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:36.580
to its patrol fleet as part of a broader EV transition. The department cited lower operating costs

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:43.580
and reduced emissions as decision factors. No specific model counts or delivery timeline were released.

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:48.760
Other municipal fleets will watch for maintenance and winter range performance data.

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:56.020
The longer wheelbase Model YL adds vehicle to load power outlets for the first time on a Tesla SUV.

00:06:56.660 --> 00:07:01.880
Reviewers noted improved rear legroom and a smoother ride over the standard Model Y.

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:07.100
The changes target family and utility buyers in right-hand drive markets.

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:13.140
Production and pricing details for other regions remain pending. The review appears in the

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:19.520
driven and highlights the added versatility for utility tasks. Observers note this marks the initial

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:27.760
rollout of V2L capability on any Tesla SUV variant. No timeline has been given for similar updates on

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:33.780
other Tesla models. Recent posts note that reported incidents involving Tesla's supervised

00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:41.020
robotaxi tests occurred only after another driver made contact. The pattern suggests the system

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:47.420
itself has not initiated collisions in the limited public data shared so far. Observers are

00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:54.280
tracking whether this holds as testing expands beyond controlled routes. A recent comment from Elon Musk

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:59.280
referenced guiding the car like an Uber driver and mentioned a three-month horizon.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:05.820
Owners are debating whether this points to an expanded summon style feature or something closer

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:12.400
to unsupervised parking. The timing follows a recent speed upgrade to the existing summon function.

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:18.820
One account highlighted ongoing friction between Tesla's FSD ambitions and European approval

00:08:18.820 --> 00:08:25.080
processes. The post noted that certain speed limit and safety rule differences continue to slow

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:32.380
rollout. This sits alongside separate national level reviews already underway. Reports show roughly

00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:39.960
90% of Amazon's disclosed EV-related holdings sit in a single non-Tesla company. The position

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:45.560
reflects a bet on a different part of the supply chain or vehicle segment. It underscores that

00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:52.240
institutional money is spreading across multiple EV plays. The disclosure appears in recent portfolio

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:58.680
filings covered by Google News. No Tesla allocation details were broken out in the same filing.

00:08:59.340 --> 00:09:05.540
The concentration highlights how large investors continue to diversify exposure beyond any single EV

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:11.560
maker. Elon Musk converted a large block of Tesla options, increasing his ownership stake.

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:17.520
The move locks in gains from earlier compensation packages and signals continued alignment with

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:23.780
the company's long-term trajectory. It comes amid ongoing discussion about future capital allocation.

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:32.420
The transaction value reached $114 billion, according to not a Tesla app. Updated ownership figures were

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:38.300
filed after the conversion. No immediate sale of shares was reported in the same filing.

00:09:39.320 --> 00:09:46.240
Now one thing worth watching is the pushback from Sweden on FSD. Sweden's transport authority

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:53.140
recommended the EU reject Tesla's supervised FSD package unless the system is altered to prevent

00:09:53.140 --> 00:09:59.480
exceeding posted speed limits. The stance adds another national voice to ongoing European reviews

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:06.040
of driver assistance rules. Tesla would need to demonstrate compliance changes before broader approval

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:11.440
can proceed. The outcome will influence whether other member states adopt similar restrictions.

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:18.900
The new suspension patent returns to a 1998 Lincoln Mark 8 layout but flips the energy budget.

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:24.580
Instead of an always active hydraulic or electromagnetic actuator fighting every bump.

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:31.640
The design lets passive air springs and dampers absorb most road inputs. Only the moments that

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:37.960
exceed the passive envelope trigger the powered element. That single change cuts continuous power draw

00:10:37.960 --> 00:10:44.220
and therefore battery energy that would otherwise be lost as heat. Every watt kept out of the

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:50.660
suspension is a watt still available for propulsion or climate control. On a vehicle whose mass is

00:10:50.660 --> 00:10:56.120
already dominated by the battery pack even modest reductions in auxiliary loads compound

00:10:56.120 --> 00:11:02.300
over a full charge cycle. Rivals that rely on fully active systems must either accept the

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:08.280
range penalty or add still more battery capacity both of which affect cost and weight.

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:15.000
Keep an eye on whether other Nordic regulators follow Denmark's approval path or align with Sweden

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:23.940
stance in the coming weeks. That covers it for today's Tesla developments. TSLA closed at $400.49

